A||N||4||chris6878||Brake Failure...||||5||
Z||000000||chris6878||04-22-2000||11:44 AM||||Hey everyone,<P>I was going to down a steep hill the other day, following traffic. This required me to use the brake alot. After finally getting to the bottom on the hill on down the road, i press the brake to stop. Well, i dont stop. I slowed down but the brakes were doing what they should. The pedal would go to the floor and barely slow the car. I figured my brakes had just got hot. But looks like the pedal wouldnt have went to the floor? i dunno...  After i got home, let her sit a while, i went out for a ride again and the brakes where fine? hmmm        are they just getting hot or what?            by the way.. new pads all way around...<P><BR>TIA<BR>chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-22-2000||12:20 PM||||Yes, you experienced high brake fade. The brakes got so hot the fluid thinned out. When you replaced the pads did you bleed the brake system? you could also have a little air in the lines. Carbomet brake pads don't get brake fade easily or upgrading your braking system to vented rotors would help a lot. Some folks don't like the carbomets due to they require more pressure when cold. If going down a steep hill you can downshift to a lower gear and use the engine to slow you down. For automatics put it in 2 instead of D.||||reg||1
Z||000002||chris6878||04-22-2000||02:45 PM||||my dad's buick somerset has vented rotors on the front (front wheel drive). It has the same bolt up pattern as my fiero because the rims will interchange.  Would this work?  just a though..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
